  "live_records": {
    "q-72088": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72088",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Solve $y$ if ${y}^{3}+5{y}^{2}-2y-10=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}+5{y}^{2}-2y-10 & = \\\\ ({y}^{3}+5{y}^{2})-(2y+10) & = \\\\ {y}^{2}(y+5)-2(y+5) & = \\\\ (y+5)\\cdot {y}^{2}-(y+5)\\cdot 2 & = \\\\ (y+5)({y}^{2}-2) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(y+5)({y}^{2}-2)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(y+5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+5 & =0 \\\\ y & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({y}^{2}-2)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-2 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =2 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-5,\\,\\pm \\sqrt{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
