    "q-114119": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114119",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find all of the real solutions to the equation ${x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+3x-15=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "We proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+3x-15 & = \\\\ ({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2})+(3x-15) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}(x-5)+3(x-5) & = \\\\ (x-5)\\cdot {x}^{2}+(x-5)\\cdot 3 & = \\\\ (x-5)({x}^{2}+3) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(x-5)({x}^{2}+3)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x-5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5 & =0 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $({x}^{2}+3)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+3) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince a squared real number cannot be negative, the equation ${x}^{2}+3=0$ has no real solutions.\n\nTherefore,  $x=5$ is the only real solution.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
